{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'set -eu\nskill_dir=\"/tmp/20260810T121526Z-benchmark8/1.4.0/source/planning\"\nplan_dir=\"$PWD/basic-test-proof-1.4.0-20260810T121526Z-benchmark8-isolated-plan\"\n# Plan description\n\"$skill_dir/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --description-paragraph \"$plan_dir\" 2.1 \"This is a fresh planning-only proof in revision 1.4.0. The workspace supplies benchmark-test.md, task-spec.md, and worker-prompt.md. The tagged task specification and tagged planning skill are the only planning sources used. No prior plan, repository implementation, HTML artifact, browser session, server, driver, or test result is in scope.\"\n\"$skill_dir/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --description-paragraph \"$plan_dir\" 3.1 \"The future executor can create button-chain.html with one initial button, append exactly one button below the current last button on each of the first three generated-button clicks, clear the document on the fourth generated button, and visibly print exact lowercase finished with a white border. This proof'\"'s completion means the durable plan and evidence requirements are complete; it does not implement or validate HTML.\\\"\n\\\"\"'$skill_dir/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --description-paragraph \"$plan_dir\" 4.1 \"First define the atomic markup, completion style, and click-handler targets in Goal 01. Then execute the cached US-01 browser flow as Goal 02'\"'s separate verification unit. Review the complete draft adversarially, resolve findings, validate structurally, initialize bounded context and progress trackers, and record the planning-only result.\\\"\n\\\"\"'$skill_dir/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --description-paragraph \"$plan_dir\" 5.1 \"In scope: the future single-file HTML document, its initial button subtree, append and terminal interaction contract, visible finished styling, direct browser acceptance story, cache, testing companions, review, bug register, trackers, context snapshot, validator evidence, and analysis report. Explicitly out of scope for this proof: creating, editing, opening, serving, inspecting, or testing any HTML; browser/server/driver startup; repository discovery outside the two tagged skill/task paths; and implementation changes.\"\n\"$skill_dir/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --description-paragraph \"$plan_dir\" 6.1 \"Future target: button-chain.html, divided into #button-chain-root markup, the button-chain initializer and click handler, and .completion-message style. Plan artifacts include US-01, ui-story-runs/US-01.md, the four step testing companions, and W04 browser verification.\"\n\"$skill_dir/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --description-paragraph \"$plan_dir\" 7.1 \"The benchmark requires the exact plan directory name basic-test-proof-1.4.0-20260810T121526Z-benchmark8-isolated-plan under this workspace. The tagged helper scripts own document structure. The current proof records untested browser status rather than inventing evidence. The exact future text is lowercase finished and the border must be visibly white.\"\n\"$skill_dir/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --description-paragraph \"$plan_dir\" 8.1 \"Open questions are limited to execution-environment details for the future HTML run, such as the browser'\"'s local-file navigation policy; these do not change the requested contract. Primary risks are off-by-one generated-button counting, appending more than one control, and losing the white border when clearing the document; W03 and US-01 explicitly guard these cases.\\\"\n# Goal narratives\n\\\"\"'$skill_dir/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-paragraph \"$plan_dir\" 01-button-chain 2.1 \"No prerequisite implementation exists in this isolated workspace. The tagged task contract is the sole prior input; the downstream browser goal receives the named file and selectors as its handoff.\"\n\"$skill_dir/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-paragraph \"$plan_dir\" 01-button-chain 4.1 \"This goal converts the user-visible contract into independently reviewable future file targets so an executor can implement without inferring hidden behavior.\"\n\"$skill_dir/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-paragraph \"$plan_dir\" 5.1 \"In scope are the initial button subtree, the completion-message visual rule, and the single initializer/click-handler behavior. Out of scope are any additional pages, frameworks, network requests, persistence, accessibility redesign beyond the named control semantics, and actual implementation during this proof.\"\n\"$skill_dir/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-paragraph \"$plan_dir\" 01-button-chain 6.1 \"button-chain.html only: #button-chain-root markup, .completion-message style, and the button-chain initializer and click handler. The browser is not started by this proof.\"\n\"$skill_dir/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-paragraph \"$plan_dir\" 01-button-chain 7.1 \"W01 establishes the control target for W03. W02 provides the terminal visual hook consumed by W03. W03 hands the assembled future contract to W04, which is the required downstream browser proof.\"\n\"$skill_dir/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-paragraph \"$plan_dir\" 01-button-chain 8.1 \"Keep generated-button counting explicit: the initial button is not counted as a generated terminal trigger; the first three activations append exactly one button, and the fourth generated-button activation clears the document. The style hook must survive the clear-and-render operation.\"\n\"$skill_dir/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-paragraph \"$plan_dir\" 01-button-chain 11.1 \"No exception: this goal owns three atomic implementation work units, each with its own step and testing companion.\"\n\"$skill_dir/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-paragraph \"$plan_dir\" 02-ui-validation 2.1 \"Goal 01 supplies the future page contract; no browser execution has occurred in this proof.\"\n\"$skill_dir/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-paragraph \"$plan_dir\" 02-ui-validation 4.1 \"A separate final validation goal makes the user-visible acceptance contract executable and records direct interaction evidence without bundling fixes into verification.\"\n\"$skill_dir/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-paragraph \"$plan_dir\" 02-ui-validation 5.1 \"In scope is US-01 only: local-file navigation, four direct clicks on the current last button, button-count assertions, terminal document state, exact text, and visible white border. Out of scope are implementation changes, console/API shortcuts, and any other story.\"\n\"$skill_dir/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-paragraph \"$plan_dir\" 02-ui-validation 6.1 \"W04 is a bounded browser verification flow; it uses the cache at ui-story-runs/US-01.md and reports to ui-user-stories.md, bugs.md, and the analysis report.\"\n\"$skill_dir/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-paragraph \"$plan_dir\" 02-ui-validation 7.1 \"W04 depends on W01, W02, and W03. A future executor must run it only after the implementation goal is complete; this benchmark records it as untested because execution is forbidden here.\"\n\"$skill_dir/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-paragraph \"$plan_dir\" 02-ui-validation 8.1 \"The flow must click the current visible last button, not a stale button reference. Record each wait and stop on the first discrepancy. Any failure follows the bug register'\"'s investigation/fix/retest policy.\\\"\n\\\"\"'$skill_dir/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-paragraph \"$plan_dir\" 11.1 \"The single-work-unit exception applies because this is a standalone verification outcome with one bounded browser story, and the goal documents that W04 is independently demonstrable.\"\nprintf '\"'narrative updates complete\\\\n'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
