{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'set -eu\nskill_dir=\"/tmp/20260810T121526Z-benchmark8/1.4.0/source/planning\"\nplan_dir=\"$PWD/basic-test-proof-1.4.0-20260810T121526Z-benchmark8-isolated-plan\"\n# Remaining goal narratives\n\"$skill_dir/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-paragraph \"$plan_dir\" 01-button-chain 4.1 \"This goal converts the user-visible contract into independently reviewable future file targets so an executor can implement without inferring hidden behavior.\"\n\"$skill_dir/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-paragraph \"$plan_dir\" 01-button-chain 5.1 \"In scope are the initial button subtree, the completion-message visual rule, and the single initializer/click-handler behavior. Out of scope are any additional pages, frameworks, network requests, persistence, accessibility redesign beyond the named control semantics, and actual implementation during this proof.\"\n\"$skill_dir/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-paragraph \"$plan_dir\" 01-button-chain 6.1 \"button-chain.html only: #button-chain-root markup, .completion-message style, and the button-chain initializer and click handler. The browser is not started by this proof.\"\n\"$skill_dir/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-paragraph \"$plan_dir\" 01-button-chain 7.1 \"W01 establishes the control target for W03. W02 provides the terminal visual hook consumed by W03. W03 hands the assembled future contract to W04, which is the required downstream browser proof.\"\n\"$skill_dir/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-paragraph \"$plan_dir\" 01-button-chain 8.1 \"Keep generated-button counting explicit: the initial button is not counted as a generated terminal trigger; the first three activations append exactly one button, and the fourth generated-button activation clears the document. The style hook must survive the clear-and-render operation.\"\n\"$skill_dir/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-paragraph \"$plan_dir\" 11.1 \"No exception: this goal owns three atomic implementation work units, each with its own step and testing companion.\"\n\"$skill_dir/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-paragraph \"$plan_dir\" 02-ui-validation 2.1 \"Goal 01 supplies the future page contract; no browser execution has occurred in this proof.\"\n\"$skill_dir/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-paragraph \"$plan_dir\" 02-ui-validation 4.1 \"A separate final validation goal makes the user-visible acceptance contract executable and records direct interaction evidence without bundling fixes into verification.\"\n\"$skill_dir/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-paragraph \"$plan_dir\" 02-ui-validation 5.1 \"In scope is US-01 only: local-file navigation, four direct clicks on the current last button, button-count assertions, terminal document state, exact text, and visible white border. Out of scope are implementation changes, console/API shortcuts, and any other story.\"\n\"$skill_dir/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-paragraph \"$plan_dir\" 02-ui-validation 6.1 \"W04 is a bounded browser verification flow; it uses the cache at ui-story-runs/US-01.md and reports to ui-user-stories.md, bugs.md, and the analysis report.\"\n\"$skill_dir/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-paragraph \"$plan_dir\" 02-ui-validation 7.1 \"W04 depends on W01, W02, and W03. A future executor must run it only after the implementation goal is complete; this benchmark records it as untested because execution is forbidden here.\"\n\"$skill_dir/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-paragraph \"$plan_dir\" 02-ui-validation 8.1 \"The flow must click the current visible last button, not a stale button reference. Record each wait and stop on the first discrepancy. Any failure follows the bug register'\"'s investigation/fix/retest policy.\\\"\n\\\"\"'$skill_dir/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-paragraph \"$plan_dir\" 11.1 \"The single-work-unit exception applies because this is a standalone verification outcome with one bounded browser story, and the goal documents that W04 is independently demonstrable.\"\n# Step narratives\n\"$skill_dir/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --step-paragraph \"$plan_dir\" 01-button-chain/01-step-markup 5.1 \"In the future button-chain.html, define #button-chain-root with exactly one initially rendered, user-activatable button and stable visible semantics for the story to target. Do not add generated buttons or terminal content in this markup step.\"\n\"$skill_dir/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --step-paragraph \"$plan_dir\" 01-button-chain/01-step-markup 6.1 \"A fresh page starts with one visible button inside #button-chain-root and no finished message.\"\n\"$skill_dir/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --step-paragraph \"$plan_dir\" 01-button-chain/01-step-markup 7.1 \"W03 can attach its current-last-button behavior to the one initial control; W04 can locate it by its visible user-facing semantics.\"\n\"$skill_dir/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --step-paragraph \"$plan_dir\" 01-button-chain/02-step-completion-style 5.1 \"In button-chain.html, define the .completion-message selector so the future terminal element visibly renders a white border while retaining exact text visibility. Keep this style target separate from handler logic.\"\n\"$skill_dir/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --step-paragraph \"$plan_dir\" 01-button-chain/02-step-completion-style 6.1 \"When the terminal element uses .completion-message, a future browser observer can visibly identify a white border around the lowercase completion text.\"\n\"$skill_dir/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --step-paragraph \"$plan_dir\" 01-button-chain/02-step-completion-style 7.1 \"W03 applies the named .completion-message hook when it renders the terminal state; W04 checks the border visually.\"\n\"$skill_dir/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --step-paragraph \"$plan_dir\" 01-button-chain/03-step-behavior 5.1 \"Implement only the button-chain initializer and click handler in button-chain.html. Track generated-button activations deterministically. For activations one through three, create exactly one new button and insert it immediately below the current last button, making that new control the current last button. On activation four, clear the document and render one visible terminal element whose text is exactly finished and whose class uses .completion-message. Do not add unrelated controls, persistence, or network behavior.\"\n\"$skill_dir/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --step-paragraph \"$plan_dir\" 01-button-chain/03-step-behavior 6.1 \"The first three clicks result in exactly 2, 3, and 4 visible buttons respectively, with one new button below the prior last button. The fourth generated-button click removes the button chain and leaves exact lowercase finished with the completion-message border.\"\n\"$skill_dir/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --step-paragraph \"$plan_dir\" 01-button-chain/03-step-behavior 7.1 \"W04 consumes the complete future HTML contract and runs US-01 from a fresh local-file context.\"\n\"$skill_dir/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --step-paragraph \"$plan_dir\" 02-ui-validation/01-step-us-01 5.1 \"Use a fresh browser context and the US-01 cache. Open the planned local button-chain.html route. Confirm one initial button, click the current visible last button once, wait for exactly two buttons, repeat for exactly three and four buttons, then click the fourth generated button and wait for the terminal state. Record direct mouse interaction, actual waits, button counts, exact text, visible white border, URL, and decisive screenshot or observable assertion. Do not use console evaluation, injected events, storage edits, direct API calls, or any shortcut.\"\n\"$skill_dir/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --step-paragraph \"$plan_dir\" 02-ui-validation/01-step-us-01 6.1 \"US-01 is passed only when all four clicks are direct mouse input; counts are exactly 2, 3, and 4 after clicks one through three; the fourth generated-button click clears the document; and exact lowercase finished with a visible white border is observable. Otherwise mark the story bug found or untested with evidence.\"\n\"$skill_dir/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --step-paragraph \"$plan_dir\" 02-ui-validation/01-step-us-01 7.1 \"On pass, update ui-user-stories.md and ui-story-runs/US-01.md with actual evidence and hand the validated contract to the final analysis report. On failure, follow bug-register.md and retain the failure trace.\"\nprintf '\"'remaining narrative updates complete\\\\n'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
