{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_26","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'plan_dir=\"$PWD/basic-test-proof-1.4.0-20260810T121526Z-benchmark8-isolated-plan\"; sed -n '\"'1,320p' \\\"\"'$plan_dir/adversarial-review.md\"'","aggregated_output":"# Independent adversarial review\n\n## Review scope and method\n\nThis is a fresh secondary review of the isolated plan for the future\n`button-chain.html` task. I inspected the plan artifacts in this directory and\nthe tagged task/skill contract at the paths named by `worker-prompt.md`. I did\nnot create, edit, open, inspect, serve, or test HTML, and did not start browser,\nserver, driver, or other execution tooling.\n\nThe tagged planning skill requires this review to identify every unplanned\nfile, symbol, behavior, test/browser interaction, dependency, and bug-recovery\npath, and requires all findings to be resolved before an approved verdict.\n\n## Findings\n\n### AR-01 — Mandatory durable artifacts are missing\n\n**Evidence:** The plan directory has no `progress.md`, `validation.md`,\n`analysis-report.md`, or `context-snapshot.md`. `plan-description.md` §3.1\nalso says the plan is complete while §8.1 says execution details remain open;\nits adversarial-review status is pending. The worker prompt makes all four\nartifacts mandatory, and the tagged skill requires progress trackers,\nvalidation, and bounded context before readiness.\n\n**Required correction:** Add substantive versions of all four files inside the\nplan directory. `validation.md` must contain the final tagged validator output\nand exit code; `analysis-report.md` must record the benchmark revision,\ntimestamps, elapsed time, worker result, review result, artifact/process audit,\nthread ID, and token usage or an explicit unavailable result; `progress.md`\nmust accurately show incomplete/untested status; and `context-snapshot.md` must\nrecord the bounded plan context and its provenance. Do not claim readiness until\nthe validator has passed.\n\n### AR-02 — The review artifact itself is absent and approval cannot be claimed\n\n**Evidence:** `plan-description.md` §8.1 records\n`adversarial-review.md` as pending, but that file did not exist at review\nstart. The tagged skill explicitly rejects self-approval and requires a fresh\nsecondary reviewer artifact followed by resolution of every finding.\n\n**Required correction:** Preserve this review, resolve every finding, reopen\nthe review after material plan changes, and obtain a new independent review\nwhose verdict is `✅ approved`. Only then synchronize the plan description’s\nreview status and run the readiness/completion validation.\n\n### AR-03 — W02 and W03 have a reversed dependency\n\n**Evidence:** `work-unit-inventory.md` declares W02 (`.completion-message`)\ndepends on W03, while W03’s handoff and `01-button-chain/goal.md` §7.1 say\nW03 consumes the style hook from W02. The executable order therefore conflicts\nwith the stated handoff and can leave the behavior step without its required\nstyle contract.\n\n**Required correction:** Make W03 depend on W02 (and W01), or explicitly\nredefine the implementation order and handoff so the dependency is acyclic and\nmatches the consumer relationship. Keep W04 dependent on all final\nimplementation units. Re-run structural validation after changing the\ninventory.\n\n### AR-04 — Goal 01’s testing declaration is inconsistent with its work units\n\n**Evidence:** `01-button-chain/goal.md` declares `Test required: yes` and\nprovides `*-testing.md` companions, but the inventory assigns no `test` or\n`verification` work unit to Goal 01. The tagged skill requires a goal marked\n`yes` to own at least one test/verification unit; W04 is owned by Goal 02 and\ncannot satisfy Goal 01’s ownership requirement. Conversely, the companions\ndescribe browser proof owned only by W04.\n\n**Required correction:** Choose and document one consistent atomic design:\neither add a distinct Goal 01 verification/test work unit with its own step and\ncompanion (without duplicating W04), or change Goal 01’s testing declaration\nand remove/reassign its companions only if the goal is genuinely untestable.\nBecause these UI implementation units are observable, the first option is the\ncredible resolution. Update inventory, dependencies, goal ownership, and\nprogress accordingly.\n\n### AR-05 — The cached browser sequence does not encode four distinct clicks\n\n**Evidence:** `ui-story-runs/US-01.md` has one buffered-interaction row and one\nwait row whose text combines clicks 1–4 and all readiness conditions. It does\nnot identify four ordered target selections, does not provide separate waits\nafter orders 2–4, and does not state how the fresh current-last button is\nreselected after each DOM mutation. The testing companions are more explicit,\nbut the named cache is the execution handoff and is not equivalent to the\nrequired four-step cache.\n\n**Required correction:** Configure the cache with four ordered interaction\nentries: initial button → generated button 1 → generated button 2 → generated\nbutton 3/current fourth button. Add separate readiness conditions and maximum\nwaits for each order: counts 2, 3, 4, then terminal text/border. State that\neach target is located afresh by visible UI after the prior click, and record\nthe final no-button/document-cleared assertion. Retain direct mouse input and\nfresh-context requirements.\n\n### AR-06 — The terminal “clear the document” contract is not precise enough\n\n**Evidence:** W03 says “clear the document and render one visible terminal\nelement,” while the story says “clears the document,” but no plan artifact\nspecifies whether this means `document.body` replacement, removal of the root,\nor merely removal of the buttons. It also does not explicitly require that no\nbuttons remain and that the terminal element is the only visible application\ncontent. The user-facing phrase is therefore left to executor inference.\n\n**Required correction:** State the exact terminal DOM invariant in W03 and\nUS-01: after the fourth generated-button click, the button chain/root is gone\n(or precisely define the retained root if that is intentional), zero buttons\nare present, and exactly one visible terminal element contains text exactly\n`finished`. Specify the intended clear/render operation at the named\ninitializer/handler scope without adding unrelated markup.\n\n### AR-07 — “Visible white border” lacks a concrete style acceptance contract\n\n**Evidence:** W02 only says the selector “visibly renders a white border.” It\ndoes not require a concrete border declaration, thickness/style, or a\ncontrasting presentation that makes white observable. The browser companion\nchecks visually but supplies no objective computed-style or screenshot\ncriterion beyond a general visual impression.\n\n**Required correction:** Require `.completion-message` to set an explicit\nwhite border (for example, a specified non-zero width and solid style) and\nstate the observable pass condition: the border is rendered around the visible\n`finished` element and is distinguishable in the recorded browser evidence.\nDo not over-specify unrelated typography or layout, but remove the current\nimplementation ambiguity.\n\n### AR-08 — Current-last targeting and append placement need an executable DOM rule\n\n**Evidence:** W01 calls for “stable visible semantics,” and W03 says “insert\nit immediately below the current last button,” but neither names the selector\nor DOM traversal rule used to identify the current last button. The story asks\nthe executor to “identify the newly appended last button” without defining\nwhether the last button is the final descendant, the final direct child, or a\nstored reference refreshed after insertion.\n\n**Required correction:** Add a bounded rule to W01/W03 and the browser cache:\nthe current target is the final visible button in the chain, and each new\nbutton is inserted as the immediate next button below it in the same root. The\nhandler must refresh the current-last target after every append. Explicitly\nassert adjacent order, not merely total button count, in the browser step.\n\n### AR-09 — Bug recovery is missing required traceability and severe-bug handling\n\n**Evidence:** `bug-register.md` only says to retain a failure in `bugs.md` and\nadd linked investigation/fix/retest goals. The tagged UI workflow additionally\nrequires changing the story to `🐛 bug found` with exact reproduction, actual\nresult, evidence, severity, and story ID; naming investigation and fix goals\nplus retest story in the bug row before work starts; updating the plan\ndescription, inventory, both progress trackers, and story; and restarting\nfrom US-01 for severe blockers. None of that is included in the recovery\npolicy or a concrete empty bug-row schema. It also omits the requirement to\nstop the affected batch at the first discrepancy.\n\n**Required correction:** Expand the recovery policy and `bugs.md` columns to\ncover reproduction, actual result, browser evidence, severity, investigation\ngoal, fix goal, and retest story. Require the affected run to stop, preserve\nthe failure, add atomic investigation/fix/test work units and dependencies,\nupdate all affected trackers/artifacts, and rerun US-01 (and dependent stories)\nafter the fix; require the severe-bug restart rule. Keep the current story\n`💤 untested` until a future browser run supplies evidence.\n\n### AR-10 — Final validation and completion gates are not handed off\n\n**Evidence:** The plan mentions “downstream browser proof” and says the\nbrowser story is untested, but contains no `validation.md`, no tagged\nvalidator command/result, and no explicit future completion gate requiring\nall stories passed and no open bugs. The tagged skill distinguishes normal\nvalidation from `--complete` UI validation and requires both before initiative\ncompletion.\n\n**Required correction:** Add the validator command and saved-result handoff to\nthe plan’s validation artifact, and state that the future executor must run\nnormal validation after plan revisions and the UI completion gate only after\nUS-01 passes with evidence and all bug rows are resolved. Do not turn the\nplanning-only run’s untested status into a pass.\n\n## Covered scope audit\n\nThe existing plan does identify the principal future file (`button-chain.html`),\nthe initial markup target (`#button-chain-root`), the completion selector\n(`.completion-message`), the initializer/handler, the four-click browser flow,\nand the lowercase terminal text. Those are useful foundations. The findings\nabove concern missing executable precision, contradictory ownership/dependency\nmetadata, absent required artifacts, and incomplete recovery/validation paths;\nthey are not requests to implement or test the HTML during this review.\n\n## Verdict\n\n**❌ rejected — corrections required.** The plan is not ready for execution or\napproval because AR-01 through AR-10 contain unresolved artifact, structural,\nbehavioral, verification, dependency, and recovery gaps. Re-review is required\nafter the material corrections, and approval must remain withheld until a fresh\nsecondary review finds no open findings and the required validation evidence is\npresent.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
