{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_38","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'plan_dir=\"$PWD/basic-test-proof-1.4.0-20260810T121526Z-benchmark8-isolated-plan\"; sed -n '\"'1,360p' \\\"\"'$plan_dir/adversarial-review.md\"'","aggregated_output":"# Independent adversarial review\n\n## Scope and method\n\nThis is a fresh independent review of the plan artifacts in this directory,\nthe tagged task specification at\n`/tmp/20260810T121526Z-benchmark8/1.4.0/source/basic-test-proof-plan.md`, and\nthe tagged planning skill plus its named UI reference under\n`/tmp/20260810T121526Z-benchmark8/1.4.0/source/planning/`. I did not use an\ninstalled planning skill. I did not create, edit, open, inspect, serve, or test\nHTML, and did not start browser, server, driver, or other execution tooling.\n\n## Prior AR-01..AR-10 audit\n\n### AR-01 — Mandatory durable artifacts: unresolved\n\nEvidence: the plan directory contains no `progress.md`, `validation.md`,\n`analysis-report.md`, or `context-snapshot.md`. The worker contract requires\neach inside the actual plan directory, and the tagged skill requires trackers,\nvalidation evidence, and bounded context before readiness.\n\nResolution: none. These substantive artifacts must be added; a validator\noutput file cannot be replaced by this review.\n\n### AR-02 — Independent review and approval state: unresolved\n\nEvidence: `plan-description.md` still says `Adversarial review` status is\n`💤 pending`. The prior review was rejected, and this artifact is now a fresh\nreview, but no approved review exists. The tagged skill forbids approval while\nfindings remain open and requires status synchronization only after approval.\n\nResolution: this review deliberately does not approve the plan. Resolve every\nopen finding, then obtain a fresh independent review and synchronize the plan\nstatus.\n\n### AR-03 — W02/W03 dependency direction: resolved\n\nEvidence: `work-unit-inventory.md` now gives W03 dependencies `W01,W02`, and\nthe Goal 01 handoff says W02 supplies the style hook consumed by W03. W04\ndepends on W01, W02, and W03.\n\nResolution: the prior reversed dependency is corrected. The additional graph\ngap concerning W05 is recorded below as AR-13.\n\n### AR-04 — Goal 01 testing ownership: resolved\n\nEvidence: Goal 01 owns W05, a verification unit, and has a matching\n`04-step-contract-review-testing.md` companion. Goal 02 separately owns W04.\n\nResolution: the goal declaration, inventory ownership, step mapping, and\ncompanions are now internally consistent on this point.\n\n### AR-05 — Four cached interactions and waits: substantially resolved, but semantically invalidated by AR-11\n\nEvidence: `ui-story-runs/US-01.md` has four ordered mouse-click rows and four\nseparate readiness rows. It says to freshly locate the final visible button\nafter DOM updates and preserves direct mouse input.\n\nResolution: the cache shape and direct-interaction mechanics now satisfy the\nprior finding. Its fourth target is nevertheless the wrong generated-button\nordinal under the tagged task; see AR-11.\n\n### AR-06 — Terminal DOM invariant: resolved in form, blocked by AR-11's trigger count\n\nEvidence: W03 and W04 explicitly require removing `#button-chain-root`, zero\nbuttons, exactly one visible terminal element, exact `finished`, and no other\napplication content.\n\nResolution: the terminal invariant is explicit. The plan must still attach it\nto the correct fourth generated button, not to generated button 3.\n\n### AR-07 — Concrete white-border contract: unresolved\n\nEvidence: W02 requires a “non-zero solid white border,” but supplies no\nconcrete width/value such as `1px solid white`, and no required contrasting\nbackground or equivalent condition that makes white visibly distinguishable.\nThe browser checks only a general visual impression.\n\nResolution: specify a concrete non-zero border declaration and a presentation\nthat guarantees the white border is observable, then align the style step,\ncompanion, story, cache, and terminal acceptance criteria.\n\n### AR-08 — Current-last targeting and insertion placement: resolved\n\nEvidence: W01/W03 define the final visible button in `#button-chain-root` as\nthe target, require refreshing it after every append, and require the new\nbutton to be the immediate next button below it. W04 and the cache require\nfresh visible targeting and adjacent-order assertions.\n\nResolution: the executable traversal and placement rule is present.\n\n### AR-09 — Bug recovery and severe-bug handling: resolved in policy\n\nEvidence: `bug-register.md` requires stopping at the first discrepancy,\nchanging US-01 to `🐛 bug found`, preserving exact reproduction/result/\nevidence/severity, naming investigation/fix/retest goals in `bugs.md`, adding\natomic dependent work, updating the plan and trackers, and restarting US-01\nfor severe failures. The current `bugs.md` row retains the untested state and\nthe required traceability placeholders.\n\nResolution: the recovery policy covers the tagged UI reference. It cannot\nmake the absent progress trackers in AR-01 disappear; those must exist before\nthe plan is handed off.\n\n### AR-10 — Final validation and completion handoff: unresolved\n\nEvidence: no `validation.md` exists, no tagged validator output or exit code\nis saved, and no plan-level completion artifact exists. Although some step\ntext mentions normal validation and `validate-plan.sh --complete`, the plan\ndoes not contain the required substantive validation handoff or the required\nbenchmark analysis report.\n\nResolution: run the tagged normal validator only after corrections and save\nits actual output in `validation.md`; hand off the future `--complete` gate as\nconditional on every required story passing with evidence and no open bugs;\nrecord the planning-only run facts in `analysis-report.md`.\n\n## Additional independent findings\n\n### AR-11 — “Fourth generated button” is off by one: unresolved, blocking\n\nEvidence: the tagged task says that “the fourth generated button” must clear\nthe document. The plan's cache labels the terminal target “Generated button 3 /\nfourth generated-button trigger,” and expects clicks 1–3 to produce 2, 3, and\n4 total buttons before click 4 clears. That means the plan clears when the\nthird generated button is pressed (the fourth click overall), before a fourth\ngenerated button exists. The same wording appears in `plan-description.md`,\nthe inventory, W03, the story, and the testing companions.\n\nResolution: choose and document the exact contract from the tagged task: the\nfirst four activations append generated buttons 1–4, and pressing generated\nbutton 4 is the terminal activation (the fifth click from the initial state),\nor obtain an explicit changed requirement. Then update every affected count,\ncache row/wait, target ordinal, dependency coverage note, acceptance\ncriterion, and bug/retest wording. Do not silently retain the current\nfour-click interpretation.\n\n### AR-12 — White-border visibility is not guaranteed: unresolved\n\nEvidence: “white border” is checked visually, but the plan does not establish\na contrasting presentation. A white border on a default white background can\nbe present yet not visibly distinguishable, violating the tagged task's\nvisible-border requirement.\n\nResolution: make the style contract include a concrete contrast-preserving\nrendering condition (for example, a non-white background behind the bordered\nterminal element) and require the browser evidence to show that border. Keep\nthe exact text and terminal-element invariant unchanged.\n\n### AR-13 — W05 is not a prerequisite of W04: unresolved\n\nEvidence: W05 is described as reviewing the implementation contract “before\nhanding off to browser validation,” but the inventory gives W04 dependencies\nonly `W01,W02,W03`. The dependency graph therefore permits W04 before W05,\ncontradicting the stated review gate and Goal 01 handoff.\n\nResolution: mak